tasks.brief:
T01 loads the page from a fixed address. Now the app asks for the address on first launch, remembers it, and explains a server it cannot reach. All of it in MainActivity.java, with views made in code (no XML layout).

1. New fields: `LinearLayout panel; TextView panelMessage; EditText addressBox; Button connectButton; boolean pageShown; boolean loadFailed;` and colours `RAISED #14171F, LINE #262B36, TEXT #F4F5F9, MUTED #8B90A3, BLUE #3B6CFF, CYAN #4CE0E8` as `static final int` made with Color.parseColor.
2. `cleanAddress` - exactly:
    static String cleanAddress(String typed) {
        String a = typed == null ? "" : typed.trim();
        if (a.length() == 0) return "";
        if (!a.matches("(?i)^https?://.*")) a = "http://" + a;
        while (a.endsWith("/")) a = a.substring(0, a.length() - 1);
        Uri u = Uri.parse(a);
        if (u.getHost() == null || u.getHost().length() == 0) return "";
        return a;
    }
3. `buildPanel()`, called in onCreate after setUpWeb(): `panel` is a vertical LinearLayout, gravity CENTER, background BG, added to `root` OVER the web view (MATCH_PARENT both ways) and hidden (`View.GONE`). Its children, top to bottom: a TextView with `getString(R.string.app_name)` (bold, 34sp, TEXT); a TextView with `getString(R.string.byline)` (14sp, MUTED); `panelMessage` (18sp, TEXT); `addressBox` (an EditText: single line, `InputType.TYPE_CLASS_TEXT | InputType.TYPE_TEXT_VARIATION_URI`, `setImeOptions(EditorInfo.IME_ACTION_GO)`, 20sp, about 460dp wide); `connectButton` (text `Connect`, `setAllCaps(false)`); a small MUTED TextView `The Menu button on the remote brings this screen back.`
   The box and the button must SHOW the remote's highlight: give each a StateListDrawable background whose `android.R.attr.state_focused` state is a rounded GradientDrawable with a 3dp CYAN stroke, and whose default state has a 1dp LINE stroke (fill RAISED for the box, BLUE for the button).
   The button's click and the box's editor action (`setOnEditorActionListener`) both call `connect()`.
4. `showPanel(String message, String address)`: set the message, put the address in the box with the caret at its end, make the panel VISIBLE, and `connectButton.requestFocus()` (OK connects at once; Up reaches the box). `hidePanel()`: if visible, GONE and `web.requestFocus()`. `panelOpen()`: is it visible.
5. `connect()`: `String a = cleanAddress(addressBox.getText().toString());` if empty: panelMessage `That is not an address. It looks like http://192.168.0.10:9191` and return. Else `server = a`, save it (`getSharedPreferences(PREFS, MODE_PRIVATE).edit().putString(KEY_SERVER, a).apply()`), panelMessage `Connecting to <a> ...`, `load()`.
6. onCreate now ends: if no address is saved, `showPanel("Where is your Lackluster Plus+ server?", getString(R.string.default_server));` (nothing is loaded yet), else `load()`.
7. The WebViewClient learns three things: `onPageStarted` sets `loadFailed = false`; `onPageFinished`: `if (loadFailed) return; pageShown = true; hidePanel();`; and an error on the MAIN page calls `failed(...)`. Both forms are needed - exactly:
            @Override
            public void onReceivedError(WebView v, WebResourceRequest req, WebResourceError err) {
                if (req.isForMainFrame()) failed(Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 23 ? String.valueOf(err.getDescription()) : "");
            }

            @Override
            @SuppressWarnings("deprecation")
            public void onReceivedError(WebView v, int code, String description, String failingUrl) {
                if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT < 23) failed(description);
            }
8. `failed` - exactly:
    void failed(String why) {
        loadFailed = true;
        pageShown = false;
        web.loadUrl("about:blank");
        String more = (why == null || why.length() == 0) ? "" : "\n(" + why + ")";
        showPanel("Cannot reach " + server + more + "\nCheck the address, and that this device is on the same network.", server);
    }
9. `load()` now starts with `loadFailed = false;`.
Then run build_apk.py until it builds.

The page is on screen (T01) and the address is asked for (T02). Now the remote and the TV's screen size. All in MainActivity.java.

1. New fields: `View customView; WebChromeClient.CustomViewCallback customViewCallback; long lastBack;` and constants `static final String KEY_WIDTH = "page_width"; static final int[] WIDTHS = {960, 1280, 1600}; static final String[] WIDTH_NAMES = {"Large", "Normal", "Small"};`
2. The TV's size. `fitPage` - exactly (call it at the end of onCreate's set-up, after buildPanel(): `fitPage(getSharedPreferences(PREFS, MODE_PRIVATE).getInt(KEY_WIDTH, 1280));`):
    /**
     * A Fire TV reports a 960 x 540 screen to a web page, which makes this page far too big. So on a TV the frame is
     * made larger than the screen and drawn reduced: the page lays itself out for a screen `width` wide.
     */
    void fitPage(int width) {
        if (!isTv()) return;
        android.util.DisplayMetrics m = new android.util.DisplayMetrics();
        getWindowManager().getDefaultDisplay().getRealMetrics(m);
        float scale = (m.widthPixels / m.density) / width;          // e.g. 960 / 1280 = 0.75
        FrameLayout.LayoutParams lp = new FrameLayout.LayoutParams(Math.round(m.widthPixels / scale), Math.round(m.heightPixels / scale));
        web.setLayoutParams(lp);
        web.setPivotX(0);
        web.setPivotY(0);
        web.setScaleX(scale);
        web.setScaleY(scale);
    }
3. Keys. `sendKeyToPage`, `back` and `dispatchKeyEvent` - exactly:
    void sendKeyToPage(String key) {
        web.evaluateJavascript("(function(){var t=document.activeElement||document.body;"
                + "t.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown',{key:'" + key + "',bubbles:true,cancelable:true}));})()", null);
    }

    void back() {
        if (customView != null) {                              // a native full-screen video: leave that first
            if (customViewCallback != null) customViewCallback.onCustomViewHidden();
            root.removeView(customView);
            customView = null;
            customViewCallback = null;
            web.requestFocus();
            return;
        }
        if (panelOpen()) {
            if (pageShown) hidePanel(); else finish();
            return;
        }
        // the page closes its own top-most thing and answers true; false means nothing was open
        web.evaluateJavascript("(function(){try{return !!(window.tvBack&&window.tvBack());}catch(e){return false;}})()",
                new ValueCallback<String>() {
                    @Override
                    public void onReceiveValue(String v) {
                        if ("true".equals(v)) return;
                        long now = System.currentTimeMillis();
                        if (now - lastBack < 2500) {
                            finish();
                        } else {
                            lastBack = now;
                            Toast.makeText(MainActivity.this, "Press Back again to leave", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();
                        }
                    }
                });
    }

    @Override
    public boolean dispatchKeyEvent(KeyEvent e) {
        int code = e.getKeyCode();
        boolean down = e.getAction() == KeyEvent.ACTION_DOWN;
        boolean first = down && e.getRepeatCount() == 0;

        if (code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BACK) {
            if (e.getAction() == KeyEvent.ACTION_UP && !e.isCanceled()) back();
            return true;
        }
        if (code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MENU) {
            if (e.getAction() == KeyEvent.ACTION_UP) menu();
            return true;
        }
        if (panelOpen() || customView != null) return super.dispatchKeyEvent(e);

        // from here on the page has the keys
        if (code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE || code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PLAY || code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PAUSE) {
            if (first) sendKeyToPage(code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PLAY ? "MediaPlay" : code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PAUSE ? "MediaPause" : "MediaPlayPause");
            return true;
        }
        if (code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_DPAD_CENTER || code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_NUMPAD_ENTER || code == KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BUTTON_A) {
            // the remote's OK reaches the page as Enter, which is what the page listens for
            return super.dispatchKeyEvent(new KeyEvent(e.getDownTime(), e.getEventTime(), e.getAction(), KeyEvent.KEYCODE_ENTER,
                    e.getRepeatCount(), e.getMetaState(), e.getDeviceId(), 0, e.getFlags(), e.getSource()));
        }
        return super.dispatchKeyEvent(e);
    }
4. The Menu list. `menu()` shows an `AlertDialog` titled with the app name whose items are, in this order, `Reload`, `Size of everything on screen`, `Change server address`, `Leave the app`, `Cancel`: 0 -> `load()`, 1 -> `pickSize()`, 2 -> `showPanel("Where is your Lackluster Plus+ server?", server)`, 3 -> `finish()`.
5. `pickSize()` - exactly:
    void pickSize() {
        final SharedPreferences prefs = getSharedPreferences(PREFS, MODE_PRIVATE);
        int now = prefs.getInt(KEY_WIDTH, 1280), at = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < WIDTHS.length; i++) if (WIDTHS[i] == now) at = i;
        new AlertDialog.Builder(this)
                .setTitle("Size of everything on screen")
                .setSingleChoiceItems(WIDTH_NAMES, at, new DialogInterface.OnClickListener() {
                    @Override
                    public void onClick(DialogInterface d, int which) {
                        prefs.edit().putInt(KEY_WIDTH, WIDTHS[which]).apply();
                        fitPage(WIDTHS[which]);
                        d.dismiss();
                    }
                })
                .show();
    }
6. A video the page puts in native full screen: `web.setWebChromeClient(new WebChromeClient() { ... })` in setUpWeb(): `onShowCustomView(View view, CustomViewCallback callback)` keeps the view and the callback and adds the view to `root` over everything (if one is already showing, call `callback.onCustomViewHidden()` and return); `onHideCustomView()` removes it, calls `customViewCallback.onCustomViewHidden()`, clears both fields and gives `web` the focus.
Imports you will need beyond T02's: android.app.AlertDialog, android.content.DialogInterface, android.content.SharedPreferences, android.view.KeyEvent, android.webkit.ValueCallback, android.webkit.WebChromeClient, android.widget.Toast.
Then run build_apk.py until it builds.
